      "message": "Yes, need more discussion. By the way, FileDescriptor hides setInt$(fd) which mainline module can\u0027t use. In the other words, we can\u0027t use a native fd to initialize a FileDescriptor object. \n```\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/libcore/ojluni/src/main/java/java/io/FileDescriptor.java;l\u003d168\n    /**\n     * @hide internal use only\n     */\n    public final void setInt$(int fd) {\n        this.descriptor \u003d fd;\n    }\n```\n\nMoreover, JNI AFileDescriptor_create() has limited on sdk level after 31\n```\nlibnativehelper/include_platform/nativehelper/JNIPlatformHelp.h:93:30: error: \u0027AFileDescriptor_create\u0027 is only available on Android 31 or newer [-Werror,-Wunguarded-availability]\n    jobject fileDescriptor \u003d AFileDescriptor_create(env);\n\n```",
